Z||000011||mrgone||08-18-2001||02:37 AM||||firstfiero, i think i can help. wrote an essay on comparing cars in that range, for my communications class.<P>BMW 325i<P>	BMW has been a benchmark among the best of the best. Their first in form and function, actively involved in many race fields that demand high skilled engineering and vehicles designed and tuned to perfection. BMW sets most of the standards in areas of performance, safety, and luxury. <BR>	For a lot of car shoppers BMW feels out of their price range, just because they have not done research and are not familiar with the BMW line of cars. BMW’s pre-owned cars are a very good buy at this time because of their uncompromising and very superior dealer maintenance. This makes the car more valuable to the buyer of a pre-owned vehicle. I also feel that most, whether a sport car nut or not, would need much more than this car has to offer. <P>	The 325i is the beefier model of the baseline 3 series, with a larger engine and more fun packed into a package more appealing than the first. A 2.5L dual overhead cam inline six, 24valve with double VANOS powerplant to be exact. VANOS being the advanced engine management system of the BMW engine. This engine places 184 happy ponies onto the grateful road @ 6000 rpm, delivered through a flawless 5 speed. Max torque is set at 175 from 3500 rpm, right where it should be. The 0 - 60 time on this car is a mere 7.6 seconds while the vehicle weighs only 3234 lbs. The turning circle distance is 34.4 feet, a few shorter than the other vehicles tested. The 4 wheel vented anti-lock discs with electronic front/rear proportioning bring this ride to a stop in a very nice distance. The interior of this vehicle can be accented with woodgrain and plush leather, heated seats, automatic dual climate control, and everything you wanted and more, for a cost. An intelligently optioned 325i (noone needs a heated steering wheel) can be had for a very acceptable price in nearly anyone’s pocketbook You can build one for yourself on their page (http://www.bmw.com) I found that the basic colours, red, black, white can be had for free, but anything but will be added for an 800 dollar charge. Other options like the upgraded CD player with disc changer can be done by brand name aftermarket audio equipment for much less, with an increase in quality.  Some neat accessories include an impressive looking aerodynamics kit that adds front skirt, ground effects, and rear boot spoiler. My finished car came out at a respectable 29,000 USD.<P>	Safety on this vehicle got a rating of ‘Good’ for overall, structure and safety cage, head and neck injury, chest injury, and legs and feet. The restraint and kinematics have a rating of acceptable. (Good is the highest rating, acceptable is second.) (http://www.crashtest.com 2001)<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">    <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B><p>[This message has been edited by mrgone (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
